msgstr "The verb is in the present because the person spoke about the present."

msgid "The verb usually keeps its tense"
msgstr "The verb usually keeps its tense"

msgid "The verb usually keeps the tense it had when it was said, so it shows when the thing was true for the speaker."
msgstr "The verb usually keeps the tense it had when it was said, so it shows when the thing was true for the speaker."

msgid "The verb usually keeps the tense it had when it was said: <0>Ta ütles, et ta on haige</0> for “I am ill”, <1>Ta ütles, et ta oli eile haige</1> for “I was ill yesterday”. English moves the verb back; Estonian usually does not."
msgstr "The verb usually keeps the tense it had when it was said: <0>Ta ütles, et ta on haige</0> for “I am ill”, <1>Ta ütles, et ta oli eile haige</1> for “I was ill yesterday”. English moves the verb back; Estonian usually does not."

